@startuml alert-delivery
title US-03: Alert Delivery - Signal Loss Persisted and Pushed to Scoped Operators

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "API\n(consuming\ninstance)" as APIConsumer
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
database "Redis\nalert-events\n(pub/sub)" as RedisPubSub
participant "API\n(all instances)" as APIAll
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Kafka -> APIConsumer : consume SIGNAL_LOSS alert\n{ alert_id, entity_id, alert_type,\n  window_start_ms, last_known_position,\n  duration_ms }

note over APIConsumer
  Kafka consumer group "api" delivers this alert
  to exactly ONE API instance. WebSocket connections
  are local per instance — direct push here would
  miss users on other instances.
end note

APIConsumer -> TSDB : INSERT INTO alerts\n( alert_id, entity_id, alert_type,\n  status, detected_at, payload )\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  alert_id = {entity_id}:SIGNAL_LOSS:{window_start_ms}
  Idempotent - safe under Kafka replay.
  Initial status = NEW.
end note

TSDB --> APIConsumer : inserted (or conflict - no-op)

APIConsumer -> RedisPubSub : PUBLISH alert-events { alert_json }

note over RedisPubSub
  All API instances subscribe to alert-events.
  Mirrors the position-updates pattern.
  Decouples Kafka consumption from WebSocket delivery.
end note

RedisPubSub --> APIAll : broadcast to all subscribers

note over APIAll
  Each instance filters by each WebSocket
  connection's saved scope before pushing.
  geo_region bounds + entity_type + alert_type
  must all match.
end note

APIAll --> Dashboard : push alert over WebSocket\n(only to connections whose scope matches)

note over Dashboard
  Alert panel updated in real time.
  Entity marker on map flagged.
  No page refresh required.
end note

Dashboard --> Operator : signal loss alert displayed\n(entity ID, last position, time dark)\nstatus: NEW

note over Operator
  Alert is raised once per loss event.
  Not re-emitted on every evaluation
  cycle while the entity remains dark.
  Operator can acknowledge or resolve
  via the alert lifecycle flow (US-13).
end note

@enduml
